# `make run-net` as a person runs it (`make test-hand-run`): the image $(KERNEL),
# the disk tools/run-disk.sh keeps, and the same QEMU command line
# (RUN_NET_CMD): interactive mode, the network without `restrict=on`. The
# Makefile turns @PORT@ and @TLSVALID@ into the ports of tools/test-httpd and
# its TLS terminator on the host's 127.0.0.1, which the guest reaches at
# 10.0.2.2. Nothing else is fetched: no name is resolved (this image's
# settings have no `net.hosts`, and SLIRP's DNS forwarder needs the host's
# resolver).
! panicked
! storage failed
! there is no volume
! the file service is gone
! fsd: mount
! first process ended
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
# A volume, mounted: the prompt is the home, not the root (TASK-26, hand-run).
< \r\n~>
# The lease takes a few hundred milliseconds under TCG.
> sleep 3\r
< \r\n~>
> net status\r
< net0  up  52:54:00:12:34:56
< address   10.0.2.15/24 (dhcp, lease
< gateway   10.0.2.2
< dns       10.0.2.3 (dhcp)
< \r\n~>
> fetch http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/\r
< Zoraya test page
< fetched over HTTP, byte for byte
< \r\n~>
# HTTPS with this image's own roots (rootfs/system/tls/roots, the production
# store): the shell grants them, `fetch` reads them and the handshake runs to
# the certificate, which the test PKI signed and no production root does.
# The full path, with the test PKI's root, is make test-net-fetch's.
> fetch https://10.0.2.2:@TLSVALID@/\r
< certificate is not signed by a trusted root
< \r\n~>
x power off
> poweroff\r
